1
00:00:11,360 --> 00:00:17,520
Aiming for the setting sun
floating over the Nakagawa,

2
00:00:18,060 --> 00:00:24,660
I kick a pebble and
even my shoe goes flying,

3
00:00:25,680 --> 00:00:33,040
onto the head of the carpenter
who was in a chokehold,

4
00:00:33,040 --> 00:00:39,140
they laughed that I'm still just a brat.

5
00:00:39,840 --> 00:00:44,220
Even if I stir up some energy somewhere,

6
00:00:44,220 --> 00:00:47,460
Katsushika, for the sake of it,
even yawns are extraordinary.

7
00:00:47,460 --> 00:00:53,180
the unused townscape is strangely gentle.

8
00:00:54,660 --> 00:01:01,140
From the pointed hat's water bottle,

9
00:01:01,860 --> 00:01:07,460
the sunset falls toward the great sky.

10
00:01:11,600 --> 00:01:15,920
Tomorrow too,
it ends just like this, doesn't it.

11
00:01:15,920 --> 00:01:21,060
Katsushika, Shibamata,
and again even happiness is lost.

12
00:01:23,060 --> 00:01:24,720
Because I'm your comrade.

13
00:01:29,320 --> 00:01:31,000
Bonus, grow up!

14
00:01:31,160 --> 00:01:31,560
2

15
00:01:39,500 --> 00:01:42,820
Men, once again the
season has finally arrived.

16
00:01:43,300 --> 00:01:47,520
Last year we were one step away,
no, one hair's width away.

17
00:01:47,520 --> 00:01:51,260
We had him cornered,
yet we failed to catch him.

18
00:01:53,080 --> 00:01:55,440
This year, we will surely catch this man

19
00:01:55,920 --> 00:01:58,820
and put an end to our long battle.

20
00:01:58,820 --> 00:01:59,620
Yeah!

21
00:01:59,620 --> 00:02:01,840
We're going to get back
every last yen he owes us!

22
00:02:01,840 --> 00:02:02,660
Yeah!

23
00:02:02,660 --> 00:02:04,200
We will definitely get it back!

24
00:02:04,200 --> 00:02:05,240
Yeah!

25
00:02:05,240 --> 00:02:06,560
Prepare yourself.

26
00:02:06,560 --> 00:02:08,320
Senior Constable Kankichi Ryotsu!

27
00:02:17,320 --> 00:02:18,740
You guys are so cool,

28
00:02:18,740 --> 00:02:19,560
you guys are so cool,

29
00:02:19,560 --> 00:02:22,240
you guys are so cool,

30
00:02:24,060 --> 00:02:24,400
I wonder.

31
00:02:29,640 --> 00:02:30,235
Well then,

32
00:02:30,285 --> 00:02:34,800
we're starting the strategy meeting
for the 23rd Ryotsu capture operation.

33
00:02:35,380 --> 00:02:38,100
Come on, there, there, no crying, no crying.

34
00:02:38,500 --> 00:02:41,440
Rikuchi-san,
did your wife run out on you again?

35
00:02:41,920 --> 00:02:44,190
If we don't go collect
the accumulated debts,

36
00:02:44,240 --> 00:02:46,560
back in the day he told me,
"You and I are divorced!"

37
00:02:46,560 --> 00:02:46,962
I also,

38
00:02:47,012 --> 00:02:51,080
the boss told me I'm fired
if I don't collect them.

39
00:02:51,740 --> 00:02:54,860
Can we really get the
money back from Ryo-san?

40
00:02:55,800 --> 00:02:58,880
Feels harder than
launching a rocket to Mars.

41
00:03:00,260 --> 00:03:01,700
What's with the defeatist talk?

42
00:03:01,700 --> 00:03:04,740
That attitude is why you'll
never get your debts back.

43
00:03:05,080 --> 00:03:07,880
Even so, do you have a good plan?

44
00:03:11,500 --> 00:03:15,160
Just in case, I've prepared a new weapon.

45
00:03:16,540 --> 00:03:18,960
Didn't that fail last year?

46
00:03:18,960 --> 00:03:20,600
Was it the "Ryo-Navi"?

47
00:03:21,080 --> 00:03:21,700
Ryo-Navi!

48
00:03:22,400 --> 00:03:25,800
That failed because we relied
solely on the transmitter's signal.

49
00:03:26,760 --> 00:03:30,232
But! This year's new weapon
takes that into account,

50
00:03:30,282 --> 00:03:31,960
and I'll make it perfect!

51
00:03:35,840 --> 00:03:39,300
We've installed surveillance cameras
in every corner of the neighborhood.

52
00:03:39,300 --> 00:03:41,711
So no matter where Ryo-san runs,

53
00:03:41,761 --> 00:03:43,540
we'll know his location instantly.

54
00:03:45,600 --> 00:03:48,640
I don't really trust machines, but I...

55
00:03:48,640 --> 00:03:49,520
It's fine!

56
00:03:51,540 --> 00:03:53,460
Operation Peeping Eye.

57
00:03:55,420 --> 00:03:56,600
Ryo-san.

58
00:03:57,200 --> 00:03:59,060
Ryo-san, at his family home.

59
00:03:59,060 --> 00:03:59,740
Yeah, yeah.

60
00:04:00,400 --> 00:04:02,460
Yeah, yeah, this time's bonus.

61
00:04:03,740 --> 00:04:05,780
Seasonal bonus: 180 and a half days' worth.

62
00:04:05,780 --> 00:04:08,380
So I finally have it in my hands.

63
00:04:08,980 --> 00:04:10,880
What a cute little bonus.

64
00:04:13,580 --> 00:04:16,340
Honestly, you should just
switch to bank transfers already.

65
00:04:16,920 --> 00:04:19,300
You're the only police officer in
the whole country who still does this.

66
00:04:21,940 --> 00:04:25,000
So, Ryo-san, what on earth are
you going to spend that bonus on?

67
00:04:25,700 --> 00:04:27,080
Don't be shocked when you hear this.

68
00:04:27,080 --> 00:04:30,060
First, I'll use this bonus as seed
money to buy a bunch of computers,

69
00:04:30,060 --> 00:04:34,000
then pour all my knowledge and
experience as a gamer into making a game.

70
00:04:34,000 --> 00:04:37,300
Then this game becomes a huge hit,
and I start a game company,

71
00:04:37,300 --> 00:04:40,360
and live a carefree life as its chairman!

72
00:04:41,300 --> 00:04:44,100
How about that? A brilliant
plan with no waste at all, right?

73
00:04:44,100 --> 00:04:47,420
I think you're the one
wasting the most money here.

74
00:04:47,420 --> 00:04:49,420
Well, I'm busy, so I'll be going now.

75
00:04:52,320 --> 00:04:56,400
Wait, the seal! Last year I got
into real trouble because of that.

76
00:04:56,980 --> 00:05:00,960
So yesterday's Goroku came in perfectly,
you know?

77
00:05:13,420 --> 00:05:16,340
That's strange,
not a single debt collector has shown up.

78
00:05:17,060 --> 00:05:20,340
Could it be they've got the bonus day wrong?

79
00:05:22,220 --> 00:05:22,880
Eek!

80
00:05:29,700 --> 00:05:37,740
Do you really think we'd get your bonus date wrong?
Right, starting now, Operation Peeping Eye begins!

81
00:05:40,760 --> 00:05:49,420
Target is currently moving west along Himawari Street at 25 kilometers per hour.
Under no circumstances let him escape, all units!

82
00:06:06,360 --> 00:06:07,520
Command car, move forward.

83
00:06:07,520 --> 00:06:10,240
Ryo-san is currently passing
through Himawari Street.

84
00:06:10,240 --> 00:06:12,320
He appears to be heading to
the Kissa Kame-no-Ana café.

85
00:06:12,320 --> 00:06:14,960
Also, Ryo-san has very keen instincts.

86
00:06:14,960 --> 00:06:17,140
Everyone, act with caution.

87
00:06:17,140 --> 00:06:17,740
Roger.

88
00:06:17,740 --> 00:06:18,480
Got it.

89
00:06:18,820 --> 00:06:19,420
Roger.

90
00:06:23,320 --> 00:06:24,500
Welcome!

91
00:06:27,520 --> 00:06:28,940
Take your time.

92
00:06:29,940 --> 00:06:33,220
But somehow it just isn't very exciting.

93
00:06:34,020 --> 00:06:35,080
Oh well.

94
00:06:38,900 --> 00:06:40,720
Team B, standby.

95
00:06:41,560 --> 00:06:43,360
Team C, ready.

96
00:06:43,360 --> 00:06:44,680
Alright!

97
00:06:44,680 --> 00:06:46,400
Commence the attack.

98
00:06:54,260 --> 00:07:10,940
!

99
00:07:12,940 --> 00:07:13,380
Well, that's good!

100
00:07:20,700 --> 00:07:22,120
What's going on? I can't see anything!

101
00:07:25,320 --> 00:07:26,960
What are you doing! Hurry up and catch him!

102
00:07:27,240 --> 00:07:28,280
Catch Ryotsu!

103
00:07:30,260 --> 00:07:31,960
Ryo-san has come out!

104
00:07:32,040 --> 00:07:32,540
I won't let you escape!

105
00:07:36,120 --> 00:07:37,180
Do your best!

106
00:07:41,100 --> 00:07:42,800
Aaaaaah!

107
00:07:42,800 --> 00:07:44,240
Aaaaaah!

108
00:07:44,240 --> 00:07:44,820
Aaaaaah!

109
00:07:49,060 --> 00:07:52,680
Ryo-san abandoned his bicycle and ran off.

110
00:07:52,680 --> 00:07:54,200
Await further instructions.

111
00:07:54,200 --> 00:07:54,740
Roger.

112
00:07:55,360 --> 00:07:57,380
As expected,
he's not going to be easy to catch.

113
00:07:58,360 --> 00:08:00,900
But no matter where he runs, it's useless.

114
00:08:01,780 --> 00:08:06,420
Your every move is being captured by countless CCD cameras
installed all over town.

115
00:08:08,180 --> 00:08:08,700
So there's no escape.

116
00:08:10,620 --> 00:08:12,660
Hey, hey.

117
00:08:12,660 --> 00:08:14,620
Whaaaat?

118
00:08:19,000 --> 00:08:21,460
Now that we've come this far,
we can finally relax.

119
00:08:21,460 --> 00:08:23,420
Whaaaat?

120
00:08:24,580 --> 00:08:28,420
That carelessness will be your downfall!
Mass-produced... why, how?

121
00:08:28,420 --> 00:08:30,540
Whaaaat?

122
00:08:32,400 --> 00:08:33,550
Aaaaah!

123
00:08:39,740 --> 00:08:42,280
Both are heading east along Sumire Street.

124
00:08:42,280 --> 00:08:42,900
Aja!

125
00:08:49,860 --> 00:08:51,940
Well, how do you want to run?

126
00:08:51,940 --> 00:08:53,080
Aaaaaah!

127
00:08:53,080 --> 00:09:07,780
Aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaah!

128
00:09:07,780 --> 00:09:10,960
You didn't go and secretly plant another tracker or something again,
did you?

129
00:09:18,120 --> 00:09:18,880
Yaah!

130
00:09:19,640 --> 00:09:20,660
Yeah, yeah, yeah!

131
00:09:20,740 --> 00:09:21,280
What? What's going on?

132
00:09:21,280 --> 00:09:22,680
Police! Police!

133
00:09:24,240 --> 00:09:25,080
Damn it!

134
00:09:35,720 --> 00:09:37,500
Aaaaaah!

135
00:09:37,500 --> 00:09:39,160
Aaaaaah!

136
00:09:43,040 --> 00:09:46,000
Right, anyone with no new developments?

137
00:09:46,760 --> 00:09:47,480
Well then,

138
00:09:47,480 --> 00:09:50,440
Eeeeeeh!

139
00:09:50,440 --> 00:09:58,100
Eeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeee!

140
00:09:58,100 --> 00:10:05,540
Eeeeh! Yes, yes!

141
00:10:09,080 --> 00:10:11,520
Look, didn't we get too close?

142
00:10:13,520 --> 00:10:16,360
A small CCD camera with a transmitter?

143
00:10:17,220 --> 00:10:19,380
I don't think that's a child's toy at all.

144
00:10:29,560 --> 00:10:30,220
Not getting away!

145
00:10:31,020 --> 00:10:32,160
Yaaah!

146
00:10:36,260 --> 00:10:37,520
My Mecha-Manbo-chan!

147
00:10:40,820 --> 00:10:43,760
Hey, Plamoya! This is your doing!

148
00:10:44,220 --> 00:10:46,160
You were using cameras to spy on me,
weren't you!

149
00:10:48,260 --> 00:10:49,160
Something like this!

150
00:10:49,800 --> 00:10:50,680
Take this!

151
00:10:53,460 --> 00:10:55,920
He's a tricky one.
This can't be the only one.

152
00:10:58,820 --> 00:11:00,540
Damn, where did he go?

153
00:11:02,120 --> 00:11:03,700
Look, he's right over there.

154
00:11:03,720 --> 00:11:04,220
Where?

155
00:11:09,760 --> 00:11:12,440
Damn, we're losing sight of Ryo-san!

156
00:11:12,800 --> 00:11:15,020
Headquarters, tell us where Ryo-san is!

157
00:11:15,020 --> 00:11:16,400
We've lost him completely.

158
00:11:16,400 --> 00:11:17,860
Headquarters, come in. Headquarters!

159
00:11:18,460 --> 00:11:20,480
Oh no, the cameras...

160
00:11:20,480 --> 00:11:22,680
The Beeping Eye operation...

161
00:11:27,280 --> 00:11:30,460
Geez, he's gone and rigged
CCD cameras all over the place!

162
00:11:31,340 --> 00:11:33,040
Well, we've mostly taken them out now.

163
00:11:34,180 --> 00:11:35,880
Right, just to be safe...

164
00:11:37,140 --> 00:11:40,440
Argh, this is unbearable.

165
00:11:40,440 --> 00:11:43,340
Operation Reaping Eye has failed!

166
00:11:43,500 --> 00:11:46,640
That's why I said we
couldn't rely on machines!

167
00:11:46,640 --> 00:11:49,440
So, does the old lady
have some good idea, then?

168
00:11:50,100 --> 00:11:51,540
Leave it to me.

169
00:11:55,700 --> 00:11:59,360
Look, they're selling
money in a place like this!

170
00:12:00,280 --> 00:12:02,340
Money, in a place like this...

171
00:12:04,040 --> 00:12:05,200
Money, money, money, money!

172
00:12:07,780 --> 00:12:09,400
Got you to look!

173
00:12:11,120 --> 00:12:12,240
A children's bank?

174
00:12:12,860 --> 00:12:15,020
Something just like this happened before...

175
00:12:16,920 --> 00:12:18,000
Just as I thought!

176
00:12:18,600 --> 00:12:20,900
We fell for the same trick as last year!

177
00:12:21,260 --> 00:12:22,220
Lend me a hand!

178
00:12:23,100 --> 00:12:25,020
See, it's easy, isn't it?

179
00:12:25,800 --> 00:12:26,600
Indeed.

180
00:12:27,260 --> 00:12:29,080
Ryo-san, please, I'm begging you.

181
00:12:29,080 --> 00:12:32,120
We're not falling for such
a simple trick over and over!

182
00:12:37,820 --> 00:12:40,340
Come on, hand over the bonus, Ryo-san.

183
00:12:40,340 --> 00:12:42,300
Fine, fine, I'll give it to you.

184
00:12:47,480 --> 00:12:50,660
Thinking you can fool us with a tearful plea again,
like last year?

185
00:12:50,660 --> 00:12:53,000
We won't fall for that this year.

186
00:12:53,000 --> 00:12:54,200
Where did it go?

187
00:12:57,880 --> 00:13:00,460
The bonus... it's gone!

188
00:13:01,720 --> 00:13:02,120
No way...

189
00:13:04,060 --> 00:13:05,940
Bonus, bonus!

190
00:13:07,860 --> 00:13:11,140
Body search! Check him thoroughly.

191
00:13:11,460 --> 00:13:15,220
A bonus envelope isn't small. If he hides it on him,
we'll find it right away.

192
00:13:17,480 --> 00:13:18,240
Damn it.

193
00:13:19,360 --> 00:13:21,080
It's not here. It's nowhere.

194
00:13:23,500 --> 00:13:25,680
Looks like he really did drop it.

195
00:13:26,500 --> 00:13:27,940
Alright! Change of plans!

196
00:13:28,240 --> 00:13:30,280
Everyone,
split up and search the whole town!

197
00:13:30,660 --> 00:13:32,280
Search every inch of the
route Ryo-san took to escape!

198
00:13:34,040 --> 00:13:34,980
Oi-ya!

199
00:13:34,980 --> 00:13:36,220
Oi-ya!

200
00:13:36,340 --> 00:13:36,980
Oi-ya!

201
00:13:37,140 --> 00:13:37,280
Oi-ya!

202
00:13:37,420 --> 00:13:38,100
Everyone!

203
00:13:38,280 --> 00:13:38,800
Everyone!

204
00:13:39,140 --> 00:13:39,640
Everyone!

205
00:13:39,640 --> 00:13:39,880
Everyone!

206
00:13:40,060 --> 00:13:40,120
Everyone!

207
00:13:40,120 --> 00:13:40,420
Everyone!

208
00:13:40,420 --> 00:13:40,600
Everyone!

209
00:13:41,240 --> 00:13:41,740
Everyone!

210
00:13:41,740 --> 00:13:41,760
Everyone!

211
00:13:41,760 --> 00:13:42,420
Everyone!

212
00:13:42,480 --> 00:13:42,600
Everyone!

213
00:13:42,600 --> 00:13:42,680
Everyone!

214
00:13:42,680 --> 00:13:42,920
Everyone!

215
00:13:42,920 --> 00:13:43,060
Everyone!

216
00:13:43,060 --> 00:13:43,520
Everyone!

217
00:13:43,520 --> 00:13:43,900
Everyone!

218
00:13:44,020 --> 00:13:44,080
Everyone!

219
00:13:44,560 --> 00:13:45,460
Everyone!

220
00:14:06,000 --> 00:14:07,360
Such a pushover, honestly.

221
00:14:07,360 --> 00:14:09,100
Falling for an act like that.

222
00:14:09,440 --> 00:14:12,140
Who'd actually drop their precious bonus?

223
00:14:17,780 --> 00:14:20,520
Better set up one more trap just in case.

224
00:14:21,120 --> 00:14:24,560
Old man, make this into
something small and inconspicuous.

225
00:14:25,900 --> 00:14:27,100
A-all of it?

226
00:14:27,980 --> 00:14:28,840
Yes, all of it.

227
00:14:28,840 --> 00:14:31,960
What happened here? Isn't this the bonus?

228
00:14:32,780 --> 00:14:34,040
This is bad, Ryo-san.

229
00:14:34,040 --> 00:14:35,700
If it gets out that we helped,

230
00:14:35,700 --> 00:14:38,020
we'll be expelled from
this shopping district.

231
00:14:38,380 --> 00:14:41,740
Hey, that urn you broke the other day,
the one we were holding for someone,

232
00:14:42,120 --> 00:14:45,580
who was it that repaired it so
you couldn't see a single scratch?

233
00:14:46,120 --> 00:14:47,080
Th-that's...

234
00:14:47,480 --> 00:14:49,820
So you won't mind if I
spill about that, then?

235
00:14:50,320 --> 00:14:51,920
Fine, fine. See ya.

236
00:14:51,920 --> 00:14:55,160
O-okay, okay, Ryo-san.

237
00:14:56,140 --> 00:14:57,260
How about this one?

238
00:14:57,260 --> 00:14:59,200
It's a ten-yen gold coin from the Meiji era.

239
00:14:59,200 --> 00:15:01,260
It's worth hundreds of
thousands at current value.

240
00:15:01,960 --> 00:15:03,260
With some sake, you could buy three of them.

241
00:15:03,980 --> 00:15:06,072
Four! Knowing you, you're exaggerating.

242
00:15:06,122 --> 00:15:08,100
You're probably fudging the count,
aren't you?

243
00:15:08,100 --> 00:15:11,440
Damn it, I can't beat you, Ryo-san.

244
00:15:12,560 --> 00:15:15,260
One coin each, inside the sandals.

245
00:15:16,280 --> 00:15:18,660
One inside the radio.

246
00:15:19,320 --> 00:15:21,960
One inside the grip.

247
00:15:25,600 --> 00:15:28,300
Once things cool off, we'll cash them in.

248
00:15:28,300 --> 00:15:31,600
If all goes well,
we might sell them for more than we paid.

249
00:15:33,420 --> 00:15:33,740
How about it?

250
00:15:46,320 --> 00:15:47,940
Damn it, what is this?

251
00:15:50,380 --> 00:16:19,320
Noooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooo!

252
00:16:21,980 --> 00:16:34,340
Aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa!

253
00:16:34,340 --> 00:16:35,960
Just my hand sticking out,
it should be somewhere around here.

254
00:16:41,420 --> 00:16:42,300
Found it.

255
00:16:43,160 --> 00:16:43,760
A silver coin.

256
00:16:43,760 --> 00:16:44,740
A silver coin.

257
00:16:44,740 --> 00:16:45,680
Hey, you!

258
00:16:45,680 --> 00:16:47,320
That cement over there, is it still...

259
00:16:57,680 --> 00:16:58,560
Dammit.

260
00:16:58,560 --> 00:17:00,520
It wasn't set yet?

261
00:17:01,960 --> 00:17:03,860
So it's quick-drying cement?

262
00:17:04,340 --> 00:17:06,880
Ugh, nngh, nnngghh!

263
00:17:07,880 --> 00:17:36,260
Nooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooo,
no no no no no no no no no no no no no no no no no no no no no no no no no no no no!

264
00:17:38,620 --> 00:17:39,680
Is it in here?

265
00:17:43,940 --> 00:17:45,360
What a house this is!

266
00:17:46,020 --> 00:17:46,820
That's...

267
00:17:47,860 --> 00:17:48,720
Excuse me.

268
00:17:48,720 --> 00:17:50,840
Please let me retrieve the dropped item.

269
00:17:56,120 --> 00:17:57,280
Yes!

270
00:17:57,280 --> 00:17:58,080
Second one!

271
00:17:59,520 --> 00:18:00,620
Two more!

272
00:18:04,020 --> 00:18:05,440
It's just a lion.

273
00:18:06,020 --> 00:18:07,360
Why is there a lion?

274
00:18:08,740 --> 00:18:10,560
It's not just one.

275
00:18:11,840 --> 00:18:14,440
Lions are felines, aren't they?

276
00:18:14,440 --> 00:18:17,040
Even as big as this, they're cats.

277
00:18:17,640 --> 00:18:19,440
Aw, how cute.

278
00:18:21,640 --> 00:18:23,760
The little one isn't cute at all.

279
00:18:25,440 --> 00:18:26,640
Ugh...

280
00:18:28,240 --> 00:18:30,040
Ow

281
00:18:39,700 --> 00:18:41,440
Lucky!

282
00:18:42,900 --> 00:18:44,340
Serves you right!

283
00:18:44,340 --> 00:18:47,880
Ugh, so annoying.

284
00:18:48,880 --> 00:18:48,900
Urgh!

285
00:18:49,280 --> 00:18:50,020
Urgh!

286
00:19:01,980 --> 00:19:02,480
Ugh!

287
00:19:02,480 --> 00:19:02,940
Ugh!

288
00:19:03,180 --> 00:19:03,940
Ugh!

289
00:19:03,940 --> 00:19:04,160
Ugh!

290
00:19:04,160 --> 00:19:04,360
Ugh!

291
00:19:05,580 --> 00:19:06,080
Ugh!

292
00:19:06,120 --> 00:19:06,540
Ugh!

293
00:19:06,560 --> 00:19:07,300
Ugh!

294
00:19:07,440 --> 00:19:07,940
Ugh!

295
00:19:13,440 --> 00:19:14,060
Yes!

296
00:19:25,200 --> 00:19:25,840
Gold coin?

297
00:19:27,000 --> 00:19:27,960
What the hell is this!

298
00:19:30,640 --> 00:19:32,160
Gold coin! Gold coin! Gold coin!

299
00:19:32,260 --> 00:19:33,360
My gold coin!

300
00:19:34,480 --> 00:19:36,900
Hey! Check your pockets,
and you lot help too!

301
00:19:37,920 --> 00:19:39,560
Where is it? One more!

302
00:19:40,380 --> 00:19:43,860
One more! One more! One more!

303
00:19:44,180 --> 00:19:46,820
One more! One more! One more!

304
00:19:46,860 --> 00:19:48,240
Where is it!

305
00:19:51,300 --> 00:19:54,320
Right, when you're stuck,
go back to the scene of the crime.

306
00:19:54,320 --> 00:19:55,900
Don't they say,
"Visit the scene a hundred times"?

307
00:19:58,711 --> 00:20:04,400
Damn! It's just one more!

308
00:20:04,700 --> 00:20:07,360
Where did it go, damn it!
I'm never giving up!

309
00:20:07,360 --> 00:20:09,480
Right, it's impossible for
it to just vanish like that.

310
00:20:09,480 --> 00:20:11,520
It has to be somewhere.

311
00:20:12,020 --> 00:20:13,200
No, it must be here somewhere!

312
00:20:15,760 --> 00:20:17,740
Did someone pick it up?

313
00:20:18,700 --> 00:20:20,780
Well, at least we still have these three.

314
00:20:21,580 --> 00:20:23,820
Damn it! Why is my luck so bad!

315
00:20:30,720 --> 00:20:31,760
No!

316
00:20:36,220 --> 00:20:39,500
Ringo-chan... well done...

317
00:20:41,160 --> 00:20:44,040
We did it! We did it, we really did it!

318
00:20:44,560 --> 00:20:47,920
Finally, finally, we've got them all down!

319
00:20:48,840 --> 00:20:51,420
Ryo-san! Ryo-san!

320
00:20:54,900 --> 00:20:56,840
Hey, everyone. What a turnout.

321
00:20:57,220 --> 00:20:59,520
Now, shall we have that bonus?

322
00:20:59,880 --> 00:21:01,820
Bonus? W-what are you talking about?

323
00:21:01,920 --> 00:21:04,600
You said you lost the bonus earlier...

324
00:21:06,200 --> 00:21:08,860
Why did you drop my bonus money!

325
00:21:09,060 --> 00:21:10,660
Stop with the bad acting.

326
00:21:11,340 --> 00:21:14,000
The old man at Inchoki-dō
confessed everything.

327
00:21:14,280 --> 00:21:16,020
S-sorry. I'm sorry, Ryo-san.

328
00:21:16,400 --> 00:21:16,720
Right?

329
00:21:17,460 --> 00:21:19,480
Now, hand over the four gold coins.

330
00:21:19,680 --> 00:21:22,200
What are you talking about?
I don't have anything.

331
00:21:22,920 --> 00:21:24,820
Or should we search your body again?

332
00:21:25,420 --> 00:21:26,980
Of course, we're going to do just that.

333
00:21:28,640 --> 00:21:31,940
Unlike bills, gold coins are small,
so we're going to search thoroughly.

334
00:21:32,600 --> 00:21:33,240
Yeah!

335
00:21:33,600 --> 00:21:34,860
Bad, bad, bad.

336
00:21:36,280 --> 00:21:37,240
Shall we get started?

337
00:21:48,720 --> 00:21:50,880
No matter how much you search,
it's not going to turn up.

338
00:21:50,880 --> 00:21:53,680
Because I really don't have it, you see.

339
00:21:54,500 --> 00:21:55,300
The real ones are

340
00:22:02,060 --> 00:22:02,900
What is it, Ryo-san?

341
00:22:02,900 --> 00:22:04,340
Are you trying to pull something again?

342
00:22:04,620 --> 00:22:05,380
No matter how you try to run,

343
00:22:06,200 --> 00:22:07,080
Choinbo-chan, you can't escape!

344
00:22:07,180 --> 00:22:10,700
N-no! M-my gold coins! My gold coins!

345
00:22:11,140 --> 00:22:13,240
Ugh, it's gone, gone, gone!

346
00:22:13,660 --> 00:22:16,840
I had placed the gold coins
on the drum can right here!

347
00:22:17,200 --> 00:22:17,840
It's true!

348
00:22:18,560 --> 00:22:21,300
This is another scheme to fool us again,
isn't it?

349
00:22:21,360 --> 00:22:24,200
No! It's true, it really is!

350
00:22:26,100 --> 00:22:28,480
Isn't that it over there?

351
00:22:28,900 --> 00:22:29,260
What?

352
00:22:36,480 --> 00:22:38,320
No, stop!

353
00:22:39,160 --> 00:22:40,860
Stop it!

354
00:23:07,700 --> 00:23:10,560
So this is the gold coin worth
several hundred thousand yen?

355
00:23:14,400 --> 00:23:17,700
But the picture and writing have worn away,
so they say it's completely worthless.

356
00:23:17,700 --> 00:23:20,420
They say all four together aren't
even worth ten thousand yen.

357
00:23:22,040 --> 00:23:22,800
Ryo-san.

358
00:23:23,540 --> 00:23:24,560
What do you want?

359
00:23:25,280 --> 00:23:27,900
If you're here for my bonus,
you can see for yourselves that it's gone.

360
00:23:27,900 --> 00:23:30,080
We talked it over together just now,

361
00:23:30,080 --> 00:23:32,560
and for now we've decided
to take that gold coin.

362
00:23:33,480 --> 00:23:35,300
Are you going to wipe out my debts?

363
00:23:36,000 --> 00:23:37,362
No, just the interest.

364
00:23:37,412 --> 00:23:40,591
It isn't really worth that much,

365
00:23:40,641 --> 00:23:43,140
but it's the least mercy we can show you.

366
00:23:43,360 --> 00:23:48,720
Next bonus, you'll pay back every bit of your debt,
so keep that in mind.

367
00:23:49,000 --> 00:23:52,020
You ogre! Devil! Heartless wretch!

368
00:23:53,120 --> 00:23:57,400
Next year,
we'll definitely collect every last yen!

369
00:24:03,940 --> 00:24:05,020
Now, listen, Chief.

370
00:24:05,380 --> 00:24:06,740
This is the TV remote,

371
00:24:07,060 --> 00:24:08,540
this is the radio remote,

372
00:24:08,540 --> 00:24:10,940
and this one here is the
air conditioner remote.

373
00:24:10,940 --> 00:24:13,440
They may all look the same,
but they're all different.

374
00:24:13,880 --> 00:24:16,260
Please don't just press buttons randomly.

375
00:24:16,600 --> 00:24:18,120
Seriously,
you're a total mechanical disaster.

376
00:24:18,660 --> 00:24:21,680
Next time: Lock-Out Syndrome, see you then.

377
00:24:30,420 --> 00:24:37,180
People say I'm a woman
who can't fall in love,

378
00:24:37,180 --> 00:24:42,980
but I have mountains of things I want to do.

379
00:24:44,240 --> 00:24:52,040
I want to ride a motorbike
across a brutal desert,

380
00:24:52,040 --> 00:24:59,160
I want to be freer than a bird.

381
00:24:59,940 --> 00:25:07,120
A lady's dreams,
changing as fast as a kaleidoscope,

382
00:25:08,820 --> 00:25:15,300
my heart's longing: sorry, wait for me.

383
00:25:15,300 --> 00:25:18,480
The future panorama

384
00:25:18,480 --> 00:25:22,200
dazzles as I dive into it.

385
00:25:23,600 --> 00:25:26,520
You understand, right?

386
00:25:26,520 --> 00:25:30,060
Sorry, wait for me.

